     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Q1 2022
1. 35 field consultants (10 women or 28%, 25 men or 72%) were trained on value chain studies and data collection to conduct value chain studies and survey, allowing for a short-term job opportunities and income generation. 
2: 
a) Selection of economic sectors through participatory processes have been completed for Aden, Hadramaut, Hodeidah and Sanaa. Six value chain studies has been finalized. 
b) On-going registration process of Small and Medium Enterprises using social media platform (e.g. Facebook, Twitter). Over 200 SMEs registered during the registration campaign in Aden (this figure is before screening processes). 
c) The business consultants have been deployed and inducted to support SMEPS activities in the targeted districts. 
3. No progress yet
4. No progress yet

Q2 2022
1. 921 (24 women or 3%, 897 men or 97%, 203 or 22% youth) have been capacitated on business and technical skills. 
2. Seven (7) value chain sectors identified in collaboration between the private sector and local authorities in Aden and Hadramaut and has reached out 921 MSMEs. 
#SMEs and Business Associations: 241 
#Smallholders/Micro-producers: 680
3. The preparatory works have initiated through workshops to map out the sectors that have the protentional to create job opportunities. With over 241 SMEs and Business Association selected for intervention, it is expected to create approximately 2,400 jobs and employment opportunities throughout the project.  
4. The preparatory works have been initiated through intensive communication between the local authorities and chamber of commerce (CoC). The Project will support 4 districts in Hadramaut by establishing business center serves as a one window system between the chamber of commerce and local authorities.

Q3:
